    "result": "I rewrote `solution.py` to address both failed gates. The 8 tests still pass, but I haven't re-run the gates, so I don't know the new CRAP or mutation numbers.\n\n- **CRAP:** `check_password` was too complex (complexity 11). Each rule is now its own small helper function, and `check_password` only does the type check and runs the rules in order. Each function should now have a CRAP score well under 10.\n- **Mutation:** most of the surviving mutants were in `_char_class`, the per-character class helper. I removed it. The classes rule now compares the password's characters against sets of lowercase letters, uppercase letters and digits, plus a check for anything outside ASCII letters and digits. That leaves no `<=` comparisons or constant return values for a mutant to change there.\n\nI didn't change the tests, since the existing boundary cases already exercise the new code.",
